---
description: Core architecture and environment rules for agentic-development-exercise. Applies to all files.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` first — it has the commands, the strictness list, and links to
`.claude/skills/` for per-task procedures.

Two rules override everything else:

1. **Derive, never duplicate.** Drizzle table -> drizzle-zod schema -> oRPC
   contract -> Express handler types, React Query hooks, SQL migration. A field
   is declared once, in `packages/contract/src/schema.ts`; work in that order.
   Never hand-write a Zod schema, type, migration, or fetch call that is
   derivable.
2. **npm only, zero infrastructure.** `nvm use && npm install && npm run dev`
   must work from a fresh clone. No Docker, daemon, database server, cloud
   account, or native build — SQLite is `node:sqlite`, never `better-sqlite3`.
   npm packages themselves are fine.

Gate: `npm run check`. No `any`, no `as`, no `!`, no default exports, no `enum`.
